            <title>[LU-17787] sanity-scrub test_12: Expected '' on ost1</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17787</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Andreas Dilger &amp;lt;adilger@whamcloud.com&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/75b37d43-1371-414d-a467-926b29a0323a" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/75b37d43-1371-414d-a467-926b29a0323a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_12 failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;(7) Expected '' on ost1
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;br/&gt;
clients: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-master/4510" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-master/4510&lt;/a&gt; - 5.14.0-362.13.1.el9_3.x86_64&lt;br/&gt;
servers: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-master/4510" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-master/4510&lt;/a&gt; - 5.14.0-362.13.1_lustre.el9.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This started failing on 2024-03-13 in this manner, and has failed 14x in 6 weeks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Note there is an bug in the error message itself, it is printing "&lt;tt&gt;Expected '$expected' on ost1&lt;/tt&gt;" but the "&lt;tt&gt;$expected&lt;/tt&gt;" variable is unset.  It should be fixed to print "&lt;tt&gt;Expected 'completed' on ost1&lt;/tt&gt;".  The same bug is in test_13, and test_19.  It might make sense to add a new "&lt;tt&gt;scrub_check_status_facet()&lt;/tt&gt;" helper that checks the status on a single facet passed as an argument, and that can be called directly by those tests, as well as inside the loop of "&lt;tt&gt;scrub_check_status()&lt;/tt&gt;".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It would also be good to increase the timeout of 6s to 30s in case these are just cases of overloaded VMs taking a longer time to finish the scrub?  Waiting a bit longer before failing the subtest is much better than taking hours to re-run the whole test session.&lt;/p&gt;





&lt;p&gt;VVVVVVV DO NOT REMOVE LINES BELOW, Added by Maloo for auto-association VVVVVVV&lt;br/&gt;
sanity-scrub test_12 - (7) Expected '' on ost1&lt;/p&gt;</description>
